    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "Stage 7.13 turns the accepted first-real-battle aftermath into one later causal NPC interaction.\n\nBehavior:\n- after the Stage 7.12 aftermath card is acknowledged, the first opening of the exact affected NPC DM emits one outcome-specific reply\n- `deny` targets Настя, `accuse_ken` targets Райхан, and `pay` targets Олег\n- reply copy is selected from persisted normalized outcome `win`, `lose`, or `interrupted`\n- opening a wrong NPC DM does not consume the pending reply\n- pending reply survives refresh\n- exact target DM consumes the reply once; reopen and later refresh do not duplicate it\n- accepted Stage 7.12 saves migrate to a pending DM reply when their stored aftermath is valid\n\nBoundary:\n- no new card, modal, currency, relationship system, battle rule, economy change, settlement change, conflict-core/API change, argument-canon change, NPC category, or broad DM rewrite\n- ordinary NPC DMs remain unchanged\n- source/docs controller, DM, and index mirrors remain byte-identical\n- compact repository-memory files are intentionally untouched until Safari verdict\n\nValidation:\n- implementation run `31103749482` PASS\n- focused dynamic matrix covers deny/win, accuse_ken/lose, pay/interrupted, pre-acknowledgement blocking, wrong-NPC isolation, refresh persistence, exact-target consumption, nested NPC-memory persistence, and no duplicate consumption\n- Stage 7.12, 7.11, 7.10, 7.9, real-battle, preunlock, causal vertical-slice, and observed-evidence regressions PASS\n- JS syntax, exact 14-file scope, source/docs parity, and protected memory boundary PASS\n\nForensic repairs during implementation:\n- focused validation caught a real stale-reference bug where consumption mutated a bridge object replaced by sanitization, leaving persisted state `pending`; the final implementation reads the record first, reacquires the active bridge, then persists `pending -> used`\n- two older cache-ownership smoke tests were correctly superseded from two references to three because Stage 7.13 adds `ui-dm.js` to the same cache ownership group\n- temporary workflow and patcher files were removed before PR creation",
